# Committing

Follow this only when the user asked for a commit. Do not push unless asked. Do not use `--no-verify`, `--amend`, or force-push unless the user explicitly asked.

## Before committing

- Stage only files that belong in this change.
- Never stage `.env`, `.env.*` (except `.env.example`), credentials, or secrets.
- If setup, scripts, env vars, folder structure, or features changed, `README.md` is part of the commit. A new or renamed env var is also reflected in `.env.example`.
- If a route in `apps/api` was added, removed, or changed, `docs/API.md` is part of the commit.
- When those docs are stale, update them first, then commit.

## Message

Conventional Commits. Subject line only, unless a short body is needed.

```
<type>(<scope>): <why, imperative, lowercase>

<optional body: what was wrong or what this unlocks>
```

- **type**: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `refactor`, `test`, or `chore`.
- **scope** is optional: `api`, `frontend`, `db`, or `docs`.
- The subject states why, stays under 72 characters, and has no trailing period.
- The body is one or two sentences when the subject is not enough. Do not list changed files.

```
feat(api): let admins reorder topics within a category
fix(frontend): keep quiz feedback when the activity is retaken
docs: record the signed upload response in the API reference
```
